spec ri05-edge-to-parent-then-update-parent-lpg: 2 sessions, 20 permutations
# RI05. The foreign-key deadlock shape: s1 and s2 each create an edge to parent p,
# then SET p.n. No step waits (F7): the second writer to p is refused at once, at the
# edge create or at the SET, and p.n holds the committed writer's value.
# Through the lpg API: AddEdge, then SetNodeProperty.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1e s1u s1c s2e s2u s2c
step s1e: lpg: AddEdge(c1, p)
step s1u: lpg: SetNodeProperty(p, n, 1)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2e: lpg: AddEdge(c2, p)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2u: lpg: SetNodeProperty(p, n, 2)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
ERROR: serialization conflict
final parent: MATCH (p:N {name:'p'}) RETURN p.n AS n
n
-
1
(1 row)
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"c1"
"c2"
"p" 
(3 rows)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src |id  |dst
----+----+---
"c1"|null|"p"
(1 row)
final dangling: <lpg: arcs touching a dead node, at a fresh snapshot>
live_arcs|dangling
---------+--------
